    "fullDescription": "<div><strong>Senior Software Developer</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div><strong>Location</strong>: Gaithersburg, MD (100% Onsite)<br />\r\n<strong>Pay Rate</strong>: $101.60 per hour<br />\r\n<strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full-Time<br />\r\n<strong>Shift:</strong> Day Shift<br />\r\nT<strong>ravel Required</strong>: No<br />\r\n<strong>Clearance Required</strong>: Active Top Secret/SCI with the ability to successfully pass a polygraph examination<br />\r\n<strong>Citizenship</strong> <strong>Requirement:</strong> U.S. Citizenship Required</div>\r\n\r\n<div> </div>\r\n\r\n<div><strong>Position Overview</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div>We are seeking an experienced Senior Software Developer to design, develop, test, deploy, and maintain enterprise software applications using modern development practices. The ideal candidate will have extensive software engineering experience, strong object-oriented programming skills, and a proven ability to deliver secure, scalable, and high-performance solutions in an Agile environment.</div>\r\n\r\n<div>The successful candidate will collaborate with product owners, Scrum Masters, architects, DevSecOps teams, and fellow developers to support mission-critical applications, drive modernization initiatives, and ensure software quality, reliability, and security.</div>\r\n\r\n<div> </div>\r\n\r\n<div><strong>Key</strong> <strong>Responsibilities</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Design, develop, test, deploy, and maintain enterprise software applications using modern development methodologies.</li>\r\n\t<li>Collaborate with Product Owners, Scrum Masters, architects, and development teams to deliver high-quality software within Agile sprints.</li>\r\n\t<li>Participate in sprint planning, backlog refinement, daily stand-ups, sprint reviews, and retrospectives.</li>\r\n\t<li>Write clean, maintainable, well-documented code in accordance with secure coding standards and industry best practices.</li>\r\n\t<li>Design and implement RESTful APIs, microservices, and distributed application architectures.</li>\r\n\t<li>Conduct code reviews and mentor junior developers to promote engineering excellence and knowledge sharing.</li>\r\n\t<li>Troubleshoot complex application issues, perform root cause analysis, and improve system reliability and performance.</li>\r\n\t<li>Develop and maintain automated unit, integration, and end-to-end tests.</li>\r\n\t<li>Partner with DevSecOps teams to implement CI/CD pipelines and automated deployment processes.</li>\r\n\t<li>Optimize application performance, scalability, and security across enterprise environments.</li>\r\n\t<li>Contribute to architecture discussions, technical roadmaps, and software modernization initiatives.</li>\r\n\t<li>Support production deployments and resolve issues in mission-critical environments.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<div><strong>Required</strong> <strong>Qualifications</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span>U.S. citizenship is required by contract.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span>Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field with 8–12 years of relevant experience, or a master's degree with 6–10 years of relevant experience.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span>Minimum of 8 years of professional software development experience.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span>Active Top Secret/SCI clearance and the ability to successfully pass a polygraph examination.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span>Strong proficiency in one or more object-oriented programming languages, including:</span>\r\n\t<ul>\r\n\t\t<li><span>Java</span></li>\r\n\t\t<li><span>C#</span></li>\r\n\t\t<li><span>Python</span></li>\r\n\t\t<li><span>C++</span></li>\r\n\t</ul>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li><span>Experience developing web-based applications and enterprise software solutions.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span>Hands-on experience designing, developing, and consuming REST APIs.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span>Experience working with relational and/or NoSQL databases.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span>Strong understanding of object-oriented design principles and software design patterns.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span>Experience using Git or other distributed version control systems.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span>Experience working in Agile Scrum or SAFe development environments.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span>Excellent analytical, debugging, and problem-solving skills.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span>Strong written and verbal communication skills.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<div><strong>Preferred</strong> <strong>Qualifications</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Experience developing cloud-native applications using AWS, Microsoft Azure, or other cloud platforms.</li>\r\n\t<li>Hands-on experience with containerization technologies, including Docker and Kubernetes.</li>\r\n\t<li>Experience designing and implementing microservices architectures.</li>\r\n\t<li>Familiarity with DevSecOps practices and CI/CD tools such as Jenkins, GitLab CI, or Azure DevOps.</li>\r\n\t<li>Experience with Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools such as Terraform or Ansible.</li>\r\n\t<li>Knowledge of message brokers such as Kafka or RabbitMQ.</li>\r\n\t<li>Experience with front-end frameworks such as React, Angular, or Vue.js.</li>\r\n\t<li>Familiarity with Elasticsearch, Redis, or other enterprise technologies.</li>\r\n\t<li>Experience with Secure Software Development Lifecycle (SSDLC) practices.</li>\r\n\t<li>Security+ certification or another DoD 8570/8140-compliant certification.</li>\r\n</ul>",
