    "fullDescription": "<strong>Position Name</strong>: Senior System Administrator<br />\r\n<strong>Location</strong>: Springfield, VA<br />\r\n<strong>Clearance Required</strong>: TS/SCI with CI Scope Poly<br />\r\n<strong>Work Schedule</strong>: Monday–Friday, within 5:00 AM – 9:00 PM EST window<br />\r\n<strong>Employment Type</strong>: Full-Time<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Position Overview</strong><br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe GEODS program is seeking a highly skilled Senior System Administrator to support mission-critical projects that directly impact national security and intelligence operations.<br />\r\nThe Geospatial Enterprise Open Data Store (GEODS) contract delivers integration, design, development, and sustainment of data services supporting Federal Government operations.<br />\r\nThe Senior System Administrator plays a key role in overseeing system testing, supporting deployment activities, collaborating with development teams, and contributing to backlog refinement and roadmap planning.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Key Responsibilities</strong>\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Access Management & Security</li>\r\n\t<li>Fulfill AWS S3 bucket access requests, ensuring proper authorization and compliance with security policies.</li>\r\n\t<li>Create and manage IAM roles and policies following least-privilege principles.</li>\r\n\t<li>Create, rotate, and manage IAM user access keys in accordance with the 90-day key rotation policy.</li>\r\n\t<li>Maintain strict access control to ensure secure cloud infrastructure operations.</li>\r\n\t<li>Monitoring & Troubleshooting</li>\r\n\t<li>Monitor system and application performance using tools such as:</li>\r\n\t<li>AWS CloudWatch</li>\r\n\t<li>Kibana / Elasticsearch</li>\r\n\t<li>Tableau</li>\r\n\t<li>Analyze logs and troubleshoot issues on AWS EC2 Linux instances.</li>\r\n\t<li>Diagnose and resolve network, DNS, and storage issues.</li>\r\n\t<li>Recommend cost optimization strategies and scalability improvements.</li>\r\n\t<li>Operational Support & Collaboration</li>\r\n\t<li>Respond to and resolve support tickets in accordance with SLAs.</li>\r\n\t<li>Support deployment activities alongside DevOps and development teams.</li>\r\n\t<li>Configure SNS topics and S3 bucket notifications based on operational needs.</li>\r\n\t<li>Collaborate with security, engineering, and operations teams to support AWS infrastructure.</li>\r\n\t<li>Develop and maintain Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) and technical documentation.</li>\r\n\t<li>Independence & Reliability</li>\r\n\t<li>Execute tasks independently with minimal supervision.</li>\r\n\t<li>Proactively identify and implement platform improvements.</li>\r\n\t<li>Demonstrate reliability, accountability, and commitment to team success.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>Tools & Technologies</strong>\r\n\r\n<div><br />\r\n<strong>Demonstrated experience with:</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>AWS (S3, EC2, IAM, SNS, CloudWatch)</li>\r\n\t<li>Linux administration</li>\r\n\t<li>Kibana / Elasticsearch</li>\r\n\t<li>Tableau</li>\r\n\t<li>DNS and networking fundamentals</li>\r\n\t<li>ServiceNow</li>\r\n\t<li>Jira</li>\r\n\t<li>Confluence</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>Education and Experience<br />\r\n<br />\r\nOne of the following combinations:</strong>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Bachelor's degree +5 years of relevant experience</li>\r\n\t<li>Associate's degree +7 years of relevant experience or minimum 8 years of relevant professional experience</li>\r\n\t<li>Required Skills and Competencies</li>\r\n\t<li>Strong AWS administration experience</li>\r\n\t<li>Experience managing IAM roles, policies, and access keys</li>\r\n\t<li>Linux system administration expertise</li>\r\n\t<li>Experience troubleshooting cloud infrastructure and applications</li>\r\n\t<li>Knowledge of networking, DNS, and storage systems</li>\r\n\t<li>Experience with incident management and ticketing systems</li>\r\n\t<li>Strong documentation and process improvement skills</li>\r\n\t<li>Ability to work independently in a mission-critical environment</li>\r\n\t<li>Strong communication and collaboration skills</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong>Work Environment</strong>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>On-site availability required Monday through Friday</li>\r\n\t<li>Fast-paced, mission-critical operational environment</li>\r\n\t<li>Collaboration across security, DevOps, engineering, and operations teams</li>\r\n\t<li>Preferred Certifications (Optional but Recommended)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n",
