    "summary": "<div><strong>Position Name: Senior DevEx Engineer<br />",
    "fullDescription": "<div><strong>Position Name: Senior DevEx Engineer<br />\r\nLocation: Vienna, VA<br />\r\nJob Type: Hybrid (3 days per week in the office)</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div><br />\r\n<strong>About the Role</strong><br />\r\nWe are seeking a visionary yet hands-on Senior Developer Experience (DevEx) Engineer to join as a founding individual contributor supporting our DevEx initiative. The mission of this role is to reduce developer cognitive load, accelerate engineering velocity, and deliver an outstanding end-to-end developer experience.<br />\r\nYou will work closely with engineering leadership, product teams, and platform engineers to modernize and optimize the entire software development lifecycle—from onboarding to deployment. Strong expertise in AI tooling is essential, as you will embed intelligent automation and developer-assist capabilities across workflows. You will also contribute to the renovation and extension of core data platforms, ensuring high observability, reliability, and actionable insights.</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br />\r\n<strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<div> </div>\r\n\r\n<div><strong>Developer Experience & Platform Engineering</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Define and own the Developer Experience roadmap for the Platform Team, aligned with organizational goals.</li>\r\n\t<li>Design, build, and maintain internal developer platforms that simplify and standardize development workflows.</li>\r\n\t<li>Work with Internal Developer Platform (IDP) tools such as Backstage, Cortex, or similar.</li>\r\n\t<li>Integrate and champion AI-powered developer tools (e.g., AI-assisted code generation, intelligent code review, automated documentation).</li>\r\n\t<li>Continuously evaluate emerging AI development tools and APIs for workflow integration.</li>\r\n\t<li>Establish and promote best practices for:\r\n\t<ul>\r\n\t\t<li>Azure DevOps CI/CD pipelines</li>\r\n\t\t<li>Local development environments</li>\r\n\t\t<li>Cloud-native deployments</li>\r\n\t</ul>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>Reduce developer cognitive load by abstracting infrastructure complexity, improving release management, and enabling self-service capabilities.</li>\r\n\t<li>Drive self-service solutions that allow engineers to provision, test, and deploy safely and autonomously.</li>\r\n\t<li>Optimize feedback loops with product teams to enable rapid iteration and higher-quality releases.</li>\r\n\t<li>Measure and improve DORA and SPACE metrics, using data to drive continuous improvement.</li>\r\n\t<li>Lead developer education and enablement initiatives, including demos, presentations, and certification of new DevEx features.</li>\r\n\t<li>Evaluate and implement security, compliance, and observability best practices across developer toolchains.</li>\r\n\t<li>Ensure secure and responsible AI tooling usage in line with organizational AI governance.</li>\r\n\t<li>Advocate for an engineering culture of continuous improvement.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<div><strong>Platform & Data Engineering</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Drive digital innovation by leveraging new technologies and methodologies to transform core data assets (SQL, NoSQL, and cloud-based platforms).</li>\r\n\t<li>Implement efficient data flows, including data pulls, transformations, and exchanges across internal and external sources.</li>\r\n\t<li>Work with complex and potentially noisy data, ensuring data consistency and collaborating with upstream teams.</li>\r\n\t<li>Define cost-efficient data storage strategies for CI/CD-related data repositories.</li>\r\n\t<li>Architect and promote reusable data assets, managing reference data catalogs and surfacing data via:</li>\r\n\t<li>Azure API Apps</li>\r\n\t<li>Modern visualization tools</li>\r\n\t<li>Aggregate and analyze structured and unstructured internal/external data to deliver actionable insights.</li>\r\n\t<li>Implement advanced monitoring, logging, and observability practices for developer workflows and data pipelines.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<div><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>8+ years of professional software engineering experience, including 3+ years in platform engineering, DevEx, or DevOps roles.</li>\r\n\t<li>Proven track record of delivering developer productivity and platform initiatives at scale.</li>\r\n\t<li>Deep experience with cloud-native development, including:\r\n\t<ul>\r\n\t\t<li>Azure DevOps</li>\r\n\t\t<li>GitHub Enterprise</li>\r\n\t\t<li>Kubernetes</li>\r\n\t\t<li>CI/CD pipelines</li>\r\n\t</ul>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>Strong expertise with AI-powered development tools (e.g., GitHub Copilot, OpenAI APIs, AI-based testing tools).</li>\r\n\t<li>Solid understanding of software delivery metrics (DORA, SPACE) and improvement methodologies.</li>\r\n\t<li>Advanced proficiency in at least one programming language (e.g., Java, Go, Python).</li>\r\n\t<li>Experience with Infrastructure as Code tools (e.g., Terraform).</li>\r\n\t<li>Demonstrated ability to build and operate new platform or DevEx functions and influence technical direction.</li>\r\n\t<li>Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, bridging infrastructure, product, and engineering teams.</li>\r\n\t<li>Extensive Azure experience, including:\r\n\t<ul>\r\n\t\t<li>Azure DevOps (ADO)</li>\r\n\t\t<li>Azure SQL and NoSQL</li>\r\n\t\t<li>Azure APIs</li>\r\n\t\t<li>Event Hub</li>\r\n\t\t<li>Stream Analytics</li>\r\n\t\t<li>Storage</li>\r\n\t\t<li>Log Analytics</li>\r\n\t</ul>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>Working knowledge of observability and logging platforms (ELK stack, Logz.io, Splunk).</li>\r\n\t<li>Strong scripting and automation skills (PowerShell, Python, YAML).</li>\r\n\t<li>Experience configuring cloud monitoring tools (Azure Application Insights, Log Analytics/KQL).</li>\r\n\t<li>AWS experience (EC2, S3, EMR) and cloud data migration exposure.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<div><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Experience working in multi-team engineering environments with a strong focus on developer enablement.</li>\r\n\t<li>Familiarity with Team Topologies and cognitive load reduction strategies.</li>\r\n\t<li>Prior experience integrating observability, monitoring, and logging into developer-facing systems.</li>\r\n\t<li>Event-driven architecture and microservices experience.</li>\r\n\t<li>Hands-on experience with secure software supply chain practices (e.g., SBOMs, artifact signing).</li>\r\n\t<li>Experience with BI tools and dashboards (e.g., Tableau, Business Objects).</li>\r\n\t<li>Familiarity with DevOps and CI/CD tooling such as Maven, Jenkins, Stash, Ansible, and Docker.</li>\r\n\t<li>Experience working with Agile methodologies (Kanban, Scrum).</li>\r\n</ul>",
    "updatedDate": "9 months ago",
