    "fullDescription": "<div>\r\n<h3 dir=\"ltr\">Job Title: Release Train Engineer<br />\r\nLocation: Alexandria, Virginia & Chantilly, Virginia <br />\r\nJob Type: On-site<br />\r\nClearance Required: Top Secret/SCI<br />\r\n </h3>\r\n\r\n<div>Job Overview:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWe are seeking a highly experienced Release Train Engineer (RTE) to lead Agile delivery and cross-team coordination in support of a mission-critical geospatial intelligence (GEOINT) program. This position is responsible for driving execution across multiple Agile teams, ensuring alignment, collaboration, and consistent delivery of value to support key national security objectives.<br />\r\nThe RTE will guide the implementation and continuous improvement of Agile principles, coordinate program-level planning and delivery, and facilitate communication across diverse teams and stakeholders. The ideal candidate combines strong leadership, organizational agility, and a deep understanding of scaled Agile frameworks to enable high-performing teams and efficient delivery of mission outcomes.<br />\r\n </div>\r\n\r\n<div>Primary Responsibilities:</div>\r\n\r\n<div> </div>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Serve as a servant leader and coach for the ART, ensuring alignment with Scaled Agile Framework (SAFe) principles and Lean-Agile best practices.</li>\r\n\t<li>Facilitate and optimize Program Increment (PI) Planning Events, ART Syncs, Inspect & Adapt workshops, and other key SAFe ceremonies across geographically distributed teams.</li>\r\n\t<li>Function as a people manager, with responsibility for performance management, professional development, mentorship, and career path development.</li>\r\n\t<li>Conduct regular 1:1s, biannual performance check-ins, and professional development planning with direct reports, proactively address employee relations and morale.</li>\r\n\t<li>Partner with Product Owners, System Architects, Scrum Masters, and technical leads refining features, prioritizing stories, removing delivery roadblocks, and optimizing flow.</li>\r\n\t<li>Track ART metrics (velocity, predictability, flow) and deliver transparent reporting to Leidos leadership and NGA stakeholders.</li>\r\n\t<li>Champion Agile best practices and promote continuous improvement of culture across Chinook development teams by identifying process gaps, implementing Lean-Agile practices, and coaching teams on SAFe principles.</li>\r\n\t<li>Lead the risk management process by identifying, escalating, and mitigating program risks in collaboration with stakeholders.</li>\r\n\t<li>Act as a leader, facilitating team dynamics, helping resolve conflicts, and fostering an environment of trust, respect, and shared purpose.</li>\r\n\t<li>Deliver regular program updates and status reports to Leidos leadership and NGA, providing insight into ART progress, risks, and valued delivered.</li>\r\n\t<li>Collaborate with NGA stakeholders to align delivery goals with mission priorities and ensure regulatory compliance.</li>\r\n\t<li>Mentor Scrum Masters and Agile team members on Agile best practices, advanced facilitation, risk management, and DevSecOps best practices.</li>\r\n\t<li>Foster a culture of transparency, collaboration, and innovation across geographically dispersed teams.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<div>Basic Qualifications:</div>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>US citizenship is required per contract.</li>\r\n\t<li>Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or related field and 12-15 years of prior relevant experience or Master's with 10-13 years of prior relevant experience.</li>\r\n\t<li>Active Top Secret with the ability to obtain SCI, as well as a Polygraph.</li>\r\n\t<li>SAFe RTE, SAFe Practice Consultant (SPC), or similar relevant certification.</li>\r\n\t<li>10+ years of experience in Agile program delivery, including 5+ years as a Release Train Engineer or equivalent role.</li>\r\n\t<li>Experience facilitating Agile/SAFe ceremonies across time zones with geographically distributed teams.</li>\r\n\t<li>Deep understanding of SAFe, Lean-Agile principles, and DevSecOps practices.</li>\r\n\t<li>Proficiency with Agile tools such as Confluence and Jira.</li>\r\n\t<li>Exceptional leadership, facilitation, and communication skills across technical and non-technical stakeholders.</li>\r\n\t<li>Experience integrating security and DevOps pipelines in high-assurance software delivery.</li>\r\n\t<li>Strong problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify and mitigate risks and blockers that may impede program success.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<div>Preferred Qualifications:</div>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Background in Continuous Integration (CI)/Continuous Delivery/Deployment (CD) integration, cloud migration, or enterprise transformation initiatives.</li>\r\n\t<li>Track record of mentoring Scrum Masters and Agile teams to higher levels of maturity.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<qb-div data-qb-element=\"re-enable-flow\" style=\"z-index: 2147483647; max-width: 1px; max-height: 1px; box-sizing: border-box; position: fixed; top: 10px; right: 10px;\">\r\n<div style=\"all: initial !important;\"><qb-div style=\"all: initial !important;\"></qb-div></div>\r\n</qb-div>",
