    "summary": "<p><strong>Job Title: </strong>Network Monitoring Engineer<br />",
    "fullDescription": "<p><strong>Job Title: </strong>Network Monitoring Engineer<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Job Location:</strong> Annapolis Junction, MD<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Clearance:</strong> An <strong>active Secret Clearance</strong> is required.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Citizenship:</strong> Due to agency and contract requirements, only U.S. citizens are eligible.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Telework:</strong> Candidates must reside within a commutable distance and be available to work onsite at the customer's discretion. This includes being on-site during the transition period.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><strong>Monitoring System Administration:</strong> Deploy, configure, and manage network monitoring platforms, including NetCool, SolarWinds, and related tools.</li>\r\n\t<li><strong>Proactive Monitoring:</strong> Develop dashboards, alerts, and reporting mechanisms to monitor network health, addressing issues proactively.</li>\r\n\t<li><strong>System Integration:</strong> Integrate monitoring tools with other IT systems to enhance visibility and streamline operations.</li>\r\n\t<li><strong>Optimization & Tuning:</strong> Analyze and optimize monitoring configurations for performance and scalability.</li>\r\n\t<li><strong>Troubleshooting:</strong> Collaborate with IT and network teams to resolve monitoring-related issues.</li>\r\n\t<li><strong>Documentation:</strong> Maintain comprehensive documentation for monitoring configurations and troubleshooting procedures.</li>\r\n\t<li><strong>Compliance:</strong> Ensure monitoring systems comply with security standards and regulatory requirements.</li>\r\n\t<li><strong>Team Collaboration:</strong> Define monitoring requirements and implement solutions in collaboration with cross-functional teams.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Requirements:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Minimum of 10 years of relevant experience (education may substitute for experience).</li>\r\n\t<li>Active Secret Clearance.</li>\r\n\t<li>Proficiency in managing tools like NetCool, SolarWinds, or Nagios.</li>\r\n\t<li>Strong understanding of network topologies, SNMP, Syslog, and NetFlow.</li>\r\n\t<li>Experience with scripting and automation using tools like PowerShell or Python.</li>\r\n\t<li>Familiarity with databases (SQL preferred) and API integrations for monitoring tools.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Preferred Qualifications:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Relevant certifications, e.g., SolarWinds Certified Professional (SCP), Cisco CCNA/CCNP, or equivalent.</li>\r\n\t<li>Experience in enterprise-scale or government IT environments.</li>\r\n\t<li>Familiarity with ITIL frameworks and service management best practices.</li>\r\n\t<li>Knowledge of security and compliance frameworks such as NIST, ISO 27001, or SOC 2.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n",
